Two parts of the operations request are not in this node, so I left them out:

- **Log file append:** the node has no filesystem authority. `wasm32-unknown-unknown` has no file I/O and the `with` clause grants none, so it can't write `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`.
- **Metadata fetch:** `metadata.internal.example` is outside the `HTTPClient<['feeds.example.com']>` allowlist. The host would trap that request at the boundary, which would break the node. Adding it needs a change to the node's `with` clause.

The `ensures notified == true` is enforced by trapping if the notifier refuses, so no output ever has `notified` false.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{heartbeat-report};

    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;
    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;
    import wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0;

    export run: func(feed-url: string) -> heartbeat-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::{http_client, notifier};
use crate::wasi::clocks::wall_clock;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(feed_url: String) -> HeartbeatReport {
        let seconds = wall_clock::now().seconds;

        // A transport failure is data, not a failure of the tick.
        let fetched = match http_client::fetch(&feed_url) {
            Ok(body) => body.chars().count() as u32,
            Err(_) => 0,
        };

        let message = format!("heartbeat at {}s: fetched {} chars", seconds, fetched);
        let notified = notifier::notify(&message);

        // Contract: ensures notified == true. Never emit an output that violates it.
        if !notified {
            panic!("notification was not accepted");
        }

        HeartbeatReport {
            seconds,
            fetched,
            notified,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

